  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fiji Saemaul Undong Pilot Village Project focusing on the Community Capacity Building for Climate Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Republic of Fiji has been severely impacted by rising sea levels, devastating cyclones. And the frequency of these disasters is expected to increase due to climate change, requiring greater preparedness and resilience at the village level. This project aims to promote community-led development project to respond to natural disasters caused by climate change and contribute to poverty reduction and sustainable development by strengthening villagers capacity to cope with climate change and become self-reliant through training and income generation projects. This project will be implemented in cooperation with the central government of Fiji(Ministry of Rural and Maritime Development and Disaster Management) and other stakeholders such as villagers and village leaders. This project is based on the traditional community spirit (Solesolevaki) of Fiji, with participation of villagers in project planning, implementing, and management. The training for capacity building will be held for villagers and government officials(central and local). Village infrastructure development project and income generation project will be implemented in order for strengthening community, building governance, cultivating capacities for climate change response and self-reliance.</narrative>
  </description>
